===Etymology 1===
[[Image:Wheat bran, tarwe zemelen.jpg|thumb|wheat bran]]
From {{inh|en|enm|bran}}, {{m|enm|branne}}, {{m|enm|bren}}, from {{der|en|fro|bren}}, {{m|fro|bran|t=bran, filth}}, from {{der|en|cel-gau|brennos|t=rotten}}, from {{der|en|cel-pro|*bragnos|t=rotten, foul}} (compare {{cog|cy|braen|t=stench}}, {{cog|ga|bréan|t=rancid}}, {{cog|wa|brin|t=excrement}}), from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰreHg-}} (compare {{cog|la|fragrāre|t=to smell strongly}}, {{cog|nl|brak|t=hound}}).

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɹæn/|a=RP,US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bran.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|æn|s=1}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[broken]] [[coat]] of the [[seed]] of [[wheat]], [[rye]], or other [[cereal]] [[grain]], separated from the [[flour]] or [[meal]] by [[sift]]ing or [[bolt]]ing; the [[coarse]], [[chaffy]] part of [[ground]] [[grain]].

